hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17745","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ismail, meaning Ibn Abi Khalid, narrated to us, from Qays ibn Aidh who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressing the people upon a camel, while an Abyssinian held its bridle."
"17746","Surayj ibn Yunus ibn Kifaya narrated to us, Abu Ismail al-Muaddib narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Aidh who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressing upon a red camel, while a black Abyssinian slave held its bridle."
